Particle Emitter Management

using ParticlesData = std::array<Renderer::Types::Particle, MAX_PARTICLES>;
ParticlesData particlesData;
int usedParticles = 0

struct ParticleRange{
    int from;
    int to;
}

std::vector<ParticleRange> freeToUseParticles

each emitter now also has ParticleRange as property

on init:

for each emitter:
    ParticleRange.from = usedParticles, ParticleRange.to = usedParticles + emitter.maxParticles
    usedParticles += emitter.maxParticles

On each frame:

Each emitter owns a range of particles, those particles are not "free" until the emitter is done.
Doesn't matter if the particle is not being drawn or computed.

A set of particles gets "freed" when:
- The emitter runs out of seconds and it's not loop=true
- The emitter gets destroyed

When the emitter is done, the ParticleRange is saved on freeToUseParticles

Every time an emitter is spawn:

The maxParticles is calculated, we ask if it can be filled only with what's on freeToUseParticles, if not, we ask if
it can be filled with freeToUseParticles + particlesData remaining. If those checks fails, we log some warning and prevent
the emitter to be created.
